{{Quote|These cadets are far from ready.|Jedi General Shaak Ti to drill [[Sergeant/Legends|sergeant]] Bric, discussing how the squad initially performed|<ref name="Clone Cadets" />}}
'''Domino Squad''' was a [[Clone trooper/Legends|clone trooper]] [[Clone cadet/Legends|cadet]] [[Squad/Legends|squad]] of the [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Galactic Republic]] on [[Kamino/Legends|Kamino]] during the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]]. After its members passed their test, the [[Citadel Challenge/Legends|Citadel Challenge]], members of the Domino Squad were transferred to an [[Rishi Station/Legends|outpost]] on [[Planet/Legends|planet]] [[Rishi/Legends|Rishi]] in the [[Outer Rim Territories/Legends|Outer Rim Territories]], where they were [[Defense of Rishi Station/Legends|attacked]] by [[BX-series droid commando/Legends|commando droids]]. The [[Cloning/Legends|clones]] were able to alert [[Galactic Republic/Legends|Galactic Republic]] forces, and the intruders were repelled.

==Description==
{{Quote|Check it out, boys. Time to watch the Dominoes fall.|Member of [[Bravo Squad (clone cadets)/Legends|Bravo Squad]]|<ref name="Clone Cadets" />}}
Members of Domino Squad were [[Cloning/Legends|clones]] of [[Mandalorian/Legends|Mandalorian]] [[Bounty hunter/Legends|bounty hunter]] [[Jango Fett/Legends|Jango Fett]]. Created on the [[Planet/Legends|planet]] [[Kamino/Legends|Kamino]], their sole purpose was to fight in the [[Grand Army of the Republic/Legends|Grand Army of the Republic]]. Around [[21 BBY/Legends|21 BBY]], during the [[Clone Wars/Legends|Clone Wars]], the members of Domino Squad began their last set of practice tests, under the command of Bounty Hunters [[Siniteen/Legends|Siniteen]] [[Drill sergeant/Legends|drill sergeant]] [[Bric/Legends|Bric]] and [[El-Les/Legends|El-Les]]. As their tests began, the members of Domino Squad could not function as a team, causing them to fail and costing them the chance of becoming [[Advanced Recon Commando/Legends|ARC troopers]] when Commander [[Colt/Legends|Colt]] came to select potential ARC trooper Candidates. After failing their test once again, they were granted a retest by the [[Jedi General/Legends|Jedi General]] in charge of training, [[Jedi Master/Legends|Jedi Master]] [[Shaak Ti/Legends|Shaak Ti]]. The morning of the training battle, [[Hevy/Legends|CT-782]] "Hevy" attempted to go AWOL, but was talked out of it by [[99/Legends|99]], a reject clone and maintenance worker. Despite the bounty hunter [[Bric/Legends|Bric]] deliberately sabotaging them during their retest they were able to work together as a team and pass their final test, the [[Citadel Challenge/Legends|Citadel Challenge]].

===After Kamino days===
After becoming battle-ready clone troopers, the clones of the former Domino Squad were sent to [[Rishi Station/Legends|Rishi Station]], which was located on the [[Rishi moon|moon]] of [[Rishi/Legends|Rishi]], where an [[Defense of Rishi Station/Legends|attack]] there [[Death/Legends|took the lives]] of Hevy, [[Droidbait/Legends|CT-00-2010]] "Droidbait" and [[Cutup/Legends|CT-4040]] "Cutup", leaving only [[Echo/Legends|CT-21-0408]] "Echo" and [[Fives/Legends|CT-5555]] "Fives".<ref name="Rookies">{{TCW|Rookies (episode)}}</ref> Several months after the destruction of the Rishi Station, Echo and Fives became ARC troopers after showing courage and skill during a Confederate [[Battle of Kamino/Legends|invasion]] of Kamino.<ref name="ARC Troopers">{{TCW|ARC Troopers (episode)}}</ref> However, during the [[Battle of Lola Sayu/Legends|rescue]] of [[Jedi/Legends|Jedi]] Master [[Even Piell/Legends|Even Piell]], who was held captive in a Confederate [[Citadel/Legends|prison]], their escape became complicated after alerting the prison's warden [[Osi Sobeck/Legends|Osi Sobeck]]. After a [[BX-series droid commando/Legends|commando droid]] commandeered a plasma turret and began opening fire on the group, Echo valiantly drew its fire away from Fives in an attempt to prevent the turret from destroying their escape craft; however, this attempt was in vain, as the turret successfully destroyed the shuttle in a fiery explosion, seemingly killing Echo in the process.<ref name="Counterattack">{{TCW|Counterattack}}</ref> This event left Fives believed to be the only surviving member of Domino Squad. Fives then continued to participate in the [[Battle of Umbara/Legends|Battle of Umbara]] under temporary Jedi [[General/Legends|General]] [[Pong Krell/Legends|Pong Krell]], and aided in exposing his true intentions. However, Fives would later go rogue after the Republic's handling of clone trooper [[Tup/Legends|CT-5385]] "Tup", and in turn would be killed by [[Fox/Legends|CC-1010]] "Fox".

